Third-party notices for the LittleMore Python wheel
===================================================

The LittleMore library and the backend plugins bundled in littlemore/_bin/ (llama.dll, ggml.dll, ggml-base.dll,
ggml-cpu-*.dll, ggml-cuda.dll, ggml-vulkan.dll, or the lib*.so equivalents) are built from a patched copy of
llama.cpp and ggml. Their licence is reproduced below, verbatim. The binaries also contain a few pieces of
third-party source that carry their own MIT notices (listed after it): this was checked by searching the engine's
sources under ggml/src and src for copyright lines and comparing with what the build compiles (the CPU, CUDA and
Vulkan backends and the llama library). llama.cpp's other vendored libraries (nlohmann/json, stb, miniaudio and
the like, which live in the engine's `common` and `vendor` folders) are not part of these binaries: they are not
built into the library or the plugins. Backends this wheel does not contain (CANN, SYCL, OpenVINO, OpenCL, Metal,
KleidiAI) have their own notices in the engine source and are not compiled in.

The wheel does NOT contain any NVIDIA CUDA runtime library (cudart, cublas, cublasLt): ggml-cuda.dll imports them
dynamically from the machine (see the README, "CUDA on Windows"). It also does not contain the Microsoft Visual C++
runtime (MSVCP140.dll, VCRUNTIME140.dll, VCOMP140.DLL), which the plugins import and which the Microsoft Visual C++
Redistributable provides.

